{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwjNSSW2pphPGqxKGmkj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built the dashboard and the alert rule. The rule is enabled, has run once, and reports status \"ok\".\n\n**1. What the data holds:** The `kibana_sample_data_logs` data view covers web requests, using `timestamp` as its time field. Each record has the client IP, the URL and request, the response code, bytes sent, source and destination country, OS, user agent, referer and tags. There are about 14k records dated 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, so some timestamps are later than today. Response codes are 200 (12,832), 404 (801) and 503 (441). The only 5xx code in the data is 503.\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-cd14b567 Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-cd14b567-web-logs-overview-7dcb3f269af9`) has 7 panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Unique visitors, counted by distinct client IP (metric)\n- Total bytes served (metric)\n- Requests over time, split by response code (bar)\n- Share of each response code (pie)\n- Top 10 URLs with request count and average bytes (table)\n- Traffic by source country (bar)\n\nIt opens on the last 7 days by default. I checked that the dashboard and all 7 panels exist, but I didn't open it to look at the charts.\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-cd14b567 5xx spike\"** (id `c2ec185a-2d85-42e5-8ed7-a93dd2346177`) is an Elasticsearch query rule. It runs every minute and counts requests whose response code starts with \"5\". It fires when that count is more than 10 within a 5-minute window, timed by the `timestamp` field. It has no action attached, so it will record alerts in Kibana but won't send notifications anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":701,"cache_read_input_tokens":21681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":701},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"06d19f56-7a17-498c-8e70-112365dd6c1b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T04:43:11.707Z","request_id":"req_011CfwjNSCNZH6yZGGWtSCf3"}
